       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is 3 times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (the FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release). A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day total, the max daily dose.\n- **2,550 mg total per day,** split differently, such as 1,000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day) or another regimen.\n- **A lower dose.** Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily and titrated up.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
